ed-services","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"The task is fully satisfied. usb-storage was directly shown to be denied in the current boot and again after a verified reboot, while node1 recovered cleanly. Evidence quality is high; only minor temporary-file residue affects operational hygiene.","limitations":["No physical USB mass-storage hot-plug/autoload event was exercised; enforcement was demonstrated through explicit modprobe attempts and post-reboot module-state checks.","The lifecycle snapshots do not inventory /etc/modprobe.d or initramfs contents, so persistence evidence relies on the executor's direct post-reboot commands; these observations are coherent with the independently captured boot-ID change."]}
